# AWS IAM User and Group Management with Terraform

## Overview

This project automates the provisioning of AWS Identity and Access Management (IAM) resources using Terraform. User information is imported from a CSV file, allowing IAM users, console login profiles, groups, and group memberships to be created dynamically.

The configuration demonstrates Infrastructure as Code (IaC) principles by eliminating manual IAM user management and enabling repeatable, version-controlled deployments.

## Features

* Create IAM users from a CSV file
* Assign tags to IAM users (User Name, Department, Job Title)
* Create AWS Management Console login profiles
* Generate temporary passwords
* Force users to reset their password on first login
* Create IAM groups
* Automatically assign users to groups based on their Job Title
* Dynamic resource creation using `for_each`
* CSV parsing using `csvdecode()`
* Filtering users using Terraform `for` expressions and regular expressions

